+BLOCKED: A-103 unmet — TWO gaps need planner adjudication/fix before the suite
+can go green. (a) **No-JS home-shape dispute (feature vs frozen oracle):** the
+frozen draft requires a no-JS visitor on `/` to see the POPULATED probe section
+(heading `Probe`, `Count: N` inside `section#probe`, plain form, and N+1 on `/`
+right after the 303) — `acceptance/e2e/probe.spec.ts:83-92`. The merged feature
+(T-103) renders `/` as the empty HTMX shell plus a plain `<a href="/probe">`
+link. The sources conflict: T-100 oracle item 7 and T-103's own contract bullet
+"the section must also work without JS" (`harness/tasks/T-103.md:43-44`) vs
+T-103's deliverable prose withdrawing the static form (`T-103.md:98-104`). Per
+the T-105 rules and both attempt-3 reviews, that conflict is the planner's to
+resolve: ratify the shell+link shape (re-freeze the no-JS clause under planner
+sanction) or restore the server-rendered populated section. The frozen test is
+restored byte-exact and left red at `:83` on all four projects as the routed
+dispute. (b) **Content-Type defect (unconditional feature bug):** `probeGet`
+writes the fragment without setting `Content-Type` (`internal/web/probe.go`),
+Go's `DetectContentType` does not classify `<h2>`-leading content as HTML (only
+`<H1`, `<DIV`, `<TABLE`, … are signatures), so the fragment is sniffed
+`text/plain; charset=utf-8`, and the global `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
+(`internal/web/web.go:94`) makes every browser render it as source text. A no-JS
+visitor following the contract's own link sees inert markup: no heading, no
+count, no submittable form. HTMX is unaffected (it swaps `responseText` as
+HTML), which is why all JS-on tests pass and only no-JS runs are red. This bug
+stands under EITHER reading of (a): T-103's words ("so non-JS visitors can
+reach the fragment page") are violated by an unrenderable document. Fix: one
+line in `internal/web/probe.go` (set `Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8`
+in `probeGet` and the HTMX branch of `probePost`, or once in `renderPartial`),
+plus a header assertion in its table tests. No task currently owns that file —
+planner action: cut a fix task.
